gamma: forget an output that disappears while night mode is off

The global-remove handler looked the removed output up in m.outputs and
returned early when it was not there. But m.outputs only holds outputs
that currently HAVE a gamma control, and SetEnabled(false) empties it --
so an output removed while night mode was off was never taken out of
availableOutputs, the list SetEnabled(true) builds new controls from.

Reproduced on a laptop whose lid-close disables the panel (eDP-1) with
night mode off: on lid-open the panel returns as a new wl_output beside
the stale one, and enabling night mode afterwards reports "enabled,
3600K" while the screen stays neutral. Toggling does not recover it;
only restarting the daemon does, because that rebuilds the list. Nothing
is logged at any point.

Now the early-return path drops the output from availableOutputs (and
outputRegNames) by registry name, matching what the normal path already
does for outputs that had a control.

